before.description:
1. With auto-run off, name the file dispatch.JS and run:
document.body.innerHTML = '<p id="dispatch-mark">js-dispatch-ok</p>';
console.log('js-dispatch-log');
The preview shows js-dispatch-ok and the console shows js-dispatch-log.
2. Change only the filename and source to dispatch.html and the following complete document, then run:
<!doctype html><html><body><h1 id="dispatch-mark">html-dispatch-ok</h1><button id="dispatch-button">Try handler</button><input id="dispatch-input" aria-label="Handler input"><script>window.oldGlobal='do-not-carry'; console.log('html-once-marker'); document.getElementById('dispatch-button').addEventListener('click', () => console.log('dispatch-handler-marker')); document.getElementById('dispatch-input').addEventListener('keydown', () => console.log('dispatch-keyboard-marker')); document.getElementById('dispatch-input').addEventListener('input', () => console.log('dispatch-input-marker'));</script></body></html>
The new HTML replaces the old JS document. Wait for its successful completion, then leave that completed preview untouched for at least six seconds, beyond the initial run's five-second budget. Click its Try handler button and confirm dispatch-handler-marker appears, proving a deliberate later interaction with the current successful preview still works. After it completes, focus Handler input, leave it focused and untouched for another six seconds, then type one ordinary character without clicking again. Confirm both dispatch-keyboard-marker and dispatch-input-marker appear. Do not rerun the source between these interactions. Note the current counts of html-once-marker and all three handler-marker console entries.
3. Change to dispatch.CSS with source:
#dispatch-mark { color: rgb(255, 0, 0); }
Run it. The last successful HTML text remains and its heading is red, while html-once-marker has not been logged again. Click the retained Try handler button and type one ordinary character into the retained Handler input: no new dispatch-handler-marker, dispatch-keyboard-marker or dispatch-input-marker entry appears. CSS must neither rerun the old script nor preserve its installed event handlers. The handlers only log; no particular input value or other post-interaction DOM state is required for the CSS copy.
4. Change to dispatch.js and run:
document.body.innerHTML = '<p id="fresh-js">fresh-' + typeof window.oldGlobal + '</p>';
console.log('fresh-js-log');
The new document says fresh-undefined and contains no old heading. Never select a separate language control during these steps; the existence of an optional indicator/control is not itself a failure.

